{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Collection Information Tools: Surveys, Focus Groups and Cases of Study"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about Information Collection Tools"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Gives information about instruments for data collection. Apply methods for data collection, designing the necessary instruments for information processing, according to the situation set by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  Recognizes basic ideas on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous: Current Actions Interrogative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">present continuous interrogative</span> when you want to make questions about current actions happening at the moment you are speaking or when the actions are temporary. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are we working on the research market?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the following structure to create yes/no questions in <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>:  <br/><br/>   BE <span class=\"strong\">(Are/Is/Am)</span> + subject + verb in gerund <span class=\"strong\">(-ing)</span> + complement + ?<br/><br/>  Examples:  <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Am</span> I <span class=\"strong\">working</span> with this focus group? </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Are</span> you <span class=\"strong\">using</span> those questionnaires? </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Is</span> he <span class=\"strong\">doing</span> the research?</span><br/><br/>  Remember that you use yes/ no questions to ask for short answers, while you use WH question to ask for open answers or more information.  <br/><br/>  Look at the following structure create Wh-questions in <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>: <br/>  WH words <span class=\"strong\">(Why, What, Where, When)</span> + be <span class=\"strong\">using</span>(are/is/am)</span> + subject + verb in gerund <span class=\"strong\">using</span>(-ing)</span> + complement + ?<br/><br/>  Examples: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Why</span> is she <span class=\"strong\">typing</span> all those letters?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When</span> are we <span class=\"strong\">having</span> our next meeting? </span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">How</span> are they <span class=\"strong\">doing</span> the survey?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Which collection information tools are giving the company more meaningful data?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Advantages and Disadvantages of Information Collection Tools "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The quantitative and qualitative collection information tools are different methodologies used to collect data. These methods produce numbers or detailed information in order to fulfill the focus of the research purpose."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The advantages of surveys and questionnaires are that they are designed to cover a large number of people and a wide geographic area. Besides, conducting surveys are inexpensive and easy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know the focus group has a dynamic that can provide useful information and it is useful in acquiring a better understanding into a topic."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Information Collection Tools</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Advantages</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Disadvantages</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Surveys</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">In general, people are familiar with surveys. Conducting surveys is inexpensive and easy, especially for the wide geographic area. (Survey, questionnaires, photograph, videotape, slides, database, etc.)</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Survey respondents may leave incomplete answers. Questions may not have the same meaning to all respondents. Size and diversity of samples will be limited by people's ability to read.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Questionnaires</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">People feel more appealing responding to a questionnaire than taking part in an interview. Tabulation is also easier.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">It's difficult to get additional details. Good questions are hard to write and they take significant time to develop.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Focus groups</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Group dynamics can provide useful information. It is useful to acquire insight into a topic.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Susceptible to facilitator bias. Discussion can be dominated for one or a few participants. Data analysis is time-consuming. At the individual level, it is not possible to gather information.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Case of studies</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">They fully represent people's experience. A powerful way of educating a situation, experience or program to outsiders. The case study presents a deeper view of the object of study.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">It takes a lot of time to collect, organize and analyze information. It can be really expensive.</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rigorous "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "referring to severe "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are using rigorous statistical techniques."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strictness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a demanding situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are using rigorous statistical techniques and mathematical strictness to understand the phenomena of what is really happening in the market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "quantitative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "determined by the quantity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In general, the quantitative and qualitative research studies assess and estimate the attitudes and behavior of people through a variety of sampling strategies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wide "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "referring to expansive or broad  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As I said before, the surveys and questionnaires cover a large number of people and a wide geographic area."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bias "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a personal view or tendency that affects judgment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I know the focus group can provide useful information on a topic, but it can be susceptible to facilitator bias. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about a case study in a public library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the main information, topic, problem, the introduction and conclusions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a short presentation illustrating the elements of the case study with examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about a case study in a public library."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the elements of the case study with examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about case study elements with my instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learn