de": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le02ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: Hello Dana, <br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Dana</span>: Hello, Gregory. Are we working on the research of the market today?<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: Yes, we are. To start, we are collecting and selecting all the data throughout different collection information tools. For instance, we are using rigorous statistical techniques and mathematical strictness to understand the phenomena of what is really happening in the market.<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Dana</span>: Are we using any specific method to collect data?<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: Well, we are collecting information on surveys, questionnaires, focus groups and case studies.<br>"}, {"time": "33000", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">  Dana</span>:What is the difference among all these methods?<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: Firstly, the surveys and questionnaires are written questions that people usually answer in a piece of paper or by e-mail. With this method, you can collect general information. Secondly, you can use the focus groups to interview a group of people to know what they think about a product. Finally, the case studies permit people to analyze deeply the context and the detailed information of a situation. In general, the quantitative and qualitative research studies assess and estimate the attitudes and behavior of people through a variety of sampling strategies.<br>"}, {"time": "73500", "image": "enpe8n1le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class= \"strong\">  Dana</span>: What are the advantages and disadvantages of these information collection methods?<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: As I said before, the surveys and questionnaires cover a large number of people and a wide geographic area. Besides, conducting surveys are inexpensive and easy. However, the respondents may leave incomplete answers; questions may not have the same meaning to all respondents, and size and diversity of sample will be limited by people's ability to read.<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Dana</span>: I know the focus group can provide useful information on a topic, but it can be susceptible to facilitator bias, and the discussion can be dominated for one or few participants.<br>\n<span class= \"strong\">  Gregory</span>: Also, the case study can represent people's experience when we teach a new product to new buyers, but it takes a lot of time to collect, organize, and analyze information which in terms of money can be expensive."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le02ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}